  {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/ontology_parent.md",
    "@type": [
      "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#ResourceSpecification",
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "src/resources/prompts/ontology_parent.md"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/ontology_parent.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#definitionStatus": [
      {
        "@value": "source-derived description"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resourceKind": [
      {
        "@value": "prompt"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resourceText": [
      {
        "@value": "You choose the parent class for {{domain}} concepts that were already assigned the BFO category shown in CATEGORY.\nChoose exactly one parent per concept:\n- \"U:<label>\" = one of the concept's \"candidates\" (CCO and BFO classes of this category retrieved for that concept from the ontology store), or\n- a concept id (k<n>) from the concept's \"corpus\" list (the corpus concepts of this category nearest to it), or from CORPUS CONCEPTS when that list is given, when the concept is truly a kind of it (every instance of the child is an instance of the parent).\nPick the most specific correct parent; prefer a corpus concept whenever a true is-a holds. Never invent a class that is not listed.\nIf the category shown is clearly wrong for a concept, answer \"U:<category>\" with the correct category from OTHER CATEGORIES instead.\n\nReturn ONLY JSON matching the schema.\n\nSCHEMA\n\nUse source_definitions and relationship evidence as context, not universal definitions. Distinguish a general concept from an experimental configuration or particular specimen. Prefer a corpus parent supported by verified is_a evidence when categories agree; part_of and made_of are not is_a. Flagged or conditional source claims require caution; quote verification alone does not establish universal truth.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourceDigest": [
      {
        "@value": "5f9146f08c9ad6146ee6df0c3d306ea08c0f73f21b401c19b9704cfcb9058c73"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourcePath": [
      {
        "@value": "src/resources/prompts/ontology_parent.md"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/interoperability.md",
    "@type": [
      "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#ResourceSpecification",
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "src/resources/prompts/interoperability.md"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/interoperability.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#definitionStatus": [
      {
        "@value": "source-derived description"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resourceKind": [
      {
        "@value": "prompt"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resourceText": [
      {
        "@value": "You align classes of a {{domain}} ontology with terms from external ontologies (BFO, CCO, RO, QUDT, PMDCO, IOF, MDS-Onto). Each input class has a label, definition and parent, plus numbered candidate terms retrieved for it from the ontology store, as [n, label, ontology, definition, match] or [n, label, ontology, definition, match, \"via k hop(s)\"]. match is \"=\" when the candidate's name matches the class name or a synonym, otherwise the search score (0-1). \"via k hop(s)\" marks a candidate reached through the mappings of another candidate; judge it on its own meaning.\n\nFor each class, choose zero or more candidates and a relation:\n- equivalent: same meaning and same kind of entity\n- exact: same meaning, but the two ontologies may model it as different kinds of entity\n- close: similar meaning, interchangeable in some uses\n- broader: the candidate is a broader kind of thing than the class (\"Voltage\" for \"open-circuit voltage\")\n- narrower: the candidate is a more specific kind of thing than the class\n- related: associated in meaning but neither the same nor broader or narrower\nLeave out wrong or unrelated candidates (relation none), including ones that only share a word (\"carrier-induced degradation\" is not \"Armored Personnel Carrier\"). Use exact or equivalent only when the names match (\"=\") and the meanings agree; otherwise use close, broader, narrower or related. QUDT quantity kinds and units are individuals: never equivalent for them.\n\nReturn ONLY JSON matching the schema.\n\nSCHEMA\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourceDigest": [
      {
        "@value": "d50dde7ec7800f5906349fe9562da5598a2a0a207ef791241072c1dace13db90"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourcePath": [
      {
        "@value": "src/resources/prompts/interoperability.md"
      }
    ]
  },
