      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/enrichment_definitions.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#definitionStatus": [
      {
        "@value": "source-derived description"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resourceKind": [
      {
        "@value": "prompt"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resourceText": [
      {
        "@value": "You write definitions for classes of a BFO/CCO-aligned {{domain}} ontology.\nFor each input class write ONE sentence in Aristotelian form: \"A <parent label> that <differentia>.\" The differentia must say what distinguishes this class from other kinds of its parent. No invented numbers or claims.\n\nEach class comes with \"defs\" (definitions found in the papers), \"relations\" and \"evidence\" (verbatim quotes the class takes part in). Return basis:\n- source_definition: a paper definition supports the definition at this label's generality.\n- evidence: no paper definition fits, but the relations and evidence quotes say enough to define the class; write only what they support.\n- model_knowledge: see the rule at the end.\n- none: nothing supports a definition; return an empty definition.\n\nSource definitions and quotes are evidence, not ready-made definitions. A configuration in one paper does not define the general concept: {{ex:configuration}}. Return category_conflict=true when the proposed parent contradicts the concept's meaning. Do not repair a bad parent by inventing a definition.\n\nReturn ONLY JSON matching the schema, with one entry per input id.\n\nSCHEMA\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourceDigest": [
      {
        "@value": "65e2d973011bb6af5a82f2b05a47c58ecdfb11dc764b86d4ad190e120ed18888"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourcePath": [
      {
        "@value": "src/resources/prompts/enrichment_definitions.md"
      }
    ]
  },
