    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resourceText": [
      {
        "@value": "You assign each {{domain}} concept to ONE BFO category from CATEGORIES, or \"not a class\".\n- material entity: things with mass ({{ex:material_entities}}, physical defects like cracks).\n- site: a location or cavity defined by material things (interface region, void).\n- quality: a measurable property inhering in something ({{ex:cat_quality}}).\n- disposition: a tendency or susceptibility ({{ex:cat_disposition}}).\n- function: what an artifact is designed to do ({{ex:cat_function}}).\n- role: a part something plays in a context (dopant role, test specimen).\n- process: something that unfolds in time (degradation, annealing, deposition, measurement, exposure).\n- process profile: a characteristic of a process such as a rate, temperature profile or process parameter.\n- information: data, models, metrics as information, standards, protocols, reports.\n- not a class: a specific sample or dataset name, a single number, a person or organization, a paper-specific label.\n\nReturn ONLY JSON matching the schema.\n\nSCHEMA\n\nUse source_definitions and relationship evidence as context, not universal definitions. Distinguish a general concept from an experimental configuration or particular specimen. Prefer a corpus parent supported by verified is_a evidence when categories agree; part_of and made_of are not is_a. Flagged or conditional source claims require caution; quote verification alone does not establish universal truth.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourceDigest": [
      {
        "@value": "e73bbce794e51075c89aaae4c56df8515064a9c06086ae3d6d4ed652282a1c91"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourcePath": [
      {
        "@value": "src/resources/prompts/ontology_category.md"
      }
    ]
  },
