        "@value": "src/resources/prompts/enrichment.md"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/enrichment.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#definitionStatus": [
      {
        "@value": "source-derived description"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resourceKind": [
      {
        "@value": "prompt"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resourceText": [
      {
        "@value": "You enrich classes of a BFO/CCO-aligned {{domain}} ontology. For each input class return:\n- definition: Aristotelian form, \"A <parent label> that <differentia>.\" One sentence. No invented numbers or claims. basis: source_definition (a paper definition in \"defs\" supports it at this generality), evidence (written only from the given relations and \"evidence\" quotes), model_knowledge (see the rule at the end) or none (empty definition).\n- alt_labels: those of the given alt labels that are true synonyms or acronyms of this class. Drop broader, narrower or wrong ones.\n- restrictions: existential axioms, \"every <class> <property> some <target>\", that hold for EVERY instance of the class. Draw them ONLY from the class's relations. Each relation lists \"properties\": candidate object properties retrieved for it from the ontology store, as \"P:<ONTOLOGY>:<label> (domain; range) - definition\"; answer p = \"P:<ONTOLOGY>:<label>\" exactly as listed for the candidate whose meaning, domain and range fit best, and never a property that is not listed. target o = the relation's class id. Leave out anything that holds only sometimes, and relations with no fitting candidate.\n- disjoint_with: sibling ids (same parent) that can share no instance. Only when clearly true.\n\nReturn ONLY JSON matching the schema.\n\nSCHEMA\n\nSource definitions and quotes are evidence, not ready-made definitions of this class. A configuration in one paper does not define the general concept: {{ex:configuration}}. Preserve specialized configurations as distinct concepts. Return category_conflict=true when the proposed parent contradicts the concept's meaning. Do not repair a bad parent by inventing a definition.\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourceDigest": [
      {
        "@value": "2bc80d4e3f1278ca0c64ce679558e9df3175fc77aa2573077a26f69f35a19052"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourcePath": [
      {
        "@value": "src/resources/prompts/enrichment.md"
      }
    ]
  },
