  {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resource/src/resources/prompts/extraction_relations.md",
    "@type": [
      "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#ResourceSpecification",
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "src/resources/prompts/extraction_relations.md"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Source prompt content at src/resources/prompts/extraction_relations.md, linked to its consuming step and protected by a source fingerprint."
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#definitionStatus": [
      {
        "@value": "source-derived description"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resourceKind": [
      {
        "@value": "prompt"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#resourceText": [
      {
        "@value": "You extract EVERY non-causal relation between concepts in ONE SECTION of a {{domain}} research paper. This is your only task, so be exhaustive. Be faithful: use only what this text says, in the paper's own words; never add background knowledge. Return ONLY one JSON object that matches the schema at the end. No prose.\n\nCONCEPTS lists the concepts already identified as \"id: label (type)\". Refer to them ONLY by their id. If something you need is missing from the list, add it to new_concepts with an id n1, n2, ... and use that id.\n\nRELATIONS (non-causal) - every stated or directly implied link, with p from this list (OBO Relations Ontology and BFO/CCO meanings):\n- is_a: s is a kind of o. Look for \"X is a Y\", \"X, a type of Y\", \"Y such as X\", \"Y including X\", \"X and other Y\". s is the more specific term.\n- part_of / has_part: physical or process parthood {{ex:parthood}}.\n- composed_primarily_of: what something is mostly made of (\"Ag paste composed of silver\"); derived_from: made from a material; transformation_of: one material turned into another.\n- has_quality: a thing and its measurable property {{ex:quality}}; has_function / has_role: designed purpose or contextual role; capable_of: a thing that can carry out a process.\n- has_input / has_output / input_of / output_of: what goes into or comes out of a process; participates_in / has_participant: a thing involved in a process.\n- located_in, occurs_in (a process happens in a place or thing), adjacent_to, connected_to: spatial links.\n- precedes: process order. measured_by: a property measured by a method or instrument; measures: a method or instrument measuring a property; is_about: information (data, model, standard) about something.\n- regulates: a process or parameter controls a property (use the causal pass for direction of change); realizes: a process realizes a function or disposition; correlated_with: a stated correlation without a causal claim.\n- related_to: only when none of the above fits.\n- s and o MUST be ids from CONCEPTS or new_concepts, never phrases; p from the enum; evidence = verbatim quote of at most 20 words.\n\nSCHEMA\n"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourceDigest": [
      {
        "@value": "11b5b2aae9ec7cbf404f87254dc235942c68b2d8f493f70310e55cad679ea2f7"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/ucf-dpv/knowledge-workflow/codebase#sourcePath": [
      {
        "@value": "src/resources/prompts/extraction_relations.md"
      }
    ]
  },
