    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "Candidates for one concept, ranked exact label matches first, then by a fused score of three signals:\nexact (a normalised label equals one of texts), fuzzy (trigram similarity, FTS5 trigram index) and cosine\n(vector against the term vectors; pass the concept's EMBED vector, or None for labels only). A candidate needs\none signal on its own (exact, fuzzy >= min_fuzzy or cosine >= min_cosine) and a fused score >= min_score;\nthe `nearest` closest terms by cosine are kept regardless (placement always sees the nearest classes).\nkinds / ontologies restrict the result (e.g. kinds=(\"class\",), ontologies=(\"CCO\", \"BFO\"))."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
